      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "The row echelon form matrix $R$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $R$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd columns.",
